from h34 import *
M=mcq;F=tf;S=short;N=num
chapter(3,'evs','making-things','Making Things',
 ('Mini and her Appooppan the potter','In a town by the sea, Mini watches her grandfather Appooppan make a clay pot. He wets the clay, pounds it, kneads it like dough and shapes it on a spinning wheel. Her mother bakes the pots in a hot kiln. Mini helps by making patterns on the pots and colouring them. This chapter shows how pots and bricks are made, how patterns come from nature and how houses are built from different materials.'),
 [('How a clay pot is made',['A pot, a piggy bank (gullak), a birdbath and a kulhad (clay cup) are made of clay.','Appooppan makes the clay wet with enough water, so it is neither too watery nor too dry. He pounds it well and kneads it like dough.','He puts the clay on a stone wheel and shapes it by spinning it. The spinning wheel lets the clay take a round shape.','The shaped pots are dried and then baked in a very hot oven called a kiln. Baking makes the pot hard and strong, so it can hold water.','Family members make patterns on the pots to make them beautiful.','We can make clay by collecting soil from a wet place, removing stones and leaves, leaving it in water for a few days, pouring off the water and kneading the clay into dough.']),
  ('Patterns in nature and art',['A pattern is a design in which shapes and lines repeat. Patterns are found everywhere in nature, such as the spots on a leopard, the stripes on a squirrel and the leaves along a neem branch.','Zebras, peacocks, cats, tigers, butterflies and fish have patterns on their bodies.','Many artists who paint pots take ideas for their patterns from nature, using the shapes and colours they see.','Indian pottery from different parts of the country is decorated with beautiful patterns.']),
  ('Brick by brick',['Bricks are made of mud, just like pots. Mud is put into a mould, a hollow shape like a cake or kulfi mould, to give the brick its shape.','A brick becomes hard when it is baked in a kiln. Bricks are used to build houses, schools and hospitals.','Rohan loves to watch the brick wall of a house being built. Each day the wall grows brick by brick, and after a few months it becomes a big building.']),
  ('Houses of different kinds',['Not all houses are made of bricks. Other materials used to build houses are stone, wood, grass, bamboo, cement and iron.','In some warm parts of our country people make traditional mud houses. These keep the house cool inside.','They use natural materials such as grass and wood, and instead of cement many people use cow dung to make smooth walls and floors. Cow dung keeps the heat out and stops insects from coming in.','Mud houses are good for the environment because they use natural materials that can return to the soil.','We should always follow safety rules where things are being made or built.'])],
 [('Why is a clay pot baked in a kiln?',[('Wet clay is soft and breaks easily.','It needs to be strong.'),('The great heat of the kiln hardens the clay.','Baking makes it hard.'),('A baked pot can hold water and be used for a long time.','That is why we bake it.')]),
  ('How are bricks made?',[('Wet mud is pressed into a mould.','The mould gives the shape.'),('The shaped bricks are dried.','Drying removes water.'),('They are baked in a kiln to become hard.','Then they can be used to build walls.')])],
 ('Tell how a clay pot is made, in order.',['Wet and knead the clay','Shape on the wheel','Dry it','Bake it in a kiln and decorate'],['A pot is made by cutting stone','Pots are baked before shaping']),
 ['Clay pots are shaped on a wheel and baked in a kiln.','Bricks are made of mud in moulds and baked.','Patterns are repeating shapes and are found in nature.','Houses can be made of bricks, mud, wood, grass and other materials.','Mud houses keep the inside cool.'],
 [M('1',1,'What is the potter\'s oven called?','Kiln',[('Wheel','The wheel shapes clay'),('Mould','A mould shapes bricks')],'A kiln bakes pots and bricks.'),
  M('2',1,'What is shaped on the spinning wheel?','Clay',[('Wood','Pots are clay'),('Glass','Pots are clay')],'The potter shapes clay.'),
  M('3',1,'What are bricks made of?','Mud',[('Plastic','Bricks are mud'),('Iron','Bricks are mud')],'Bricks are made of mud and baked.'),
  M('4',1,'What shapes a brick?','A mould',[('A wheel','A wheel shapes pots'),('A brush','A brush paints')],'Mud is pressed into a mould.'),
  M('5',2,'Why is a pot baked?','To make it hard and strong',[('To make it soft','Baking hardens it'),('To make it wet','Baking dries it')],'Baking hardens clay.'),
  F('6',2,'Patterns are found in nature.',True,'Spots, stripes and leaves have patterns.'),
  M('7',2,'Which animal has stripes?','Zebra',[('Cow','A cow usually has patches'),('Parrot','A parrot is green')],'A zebra has stripes.'),
  M('8',2,'Why do traditional mud houses stay cool?','Mud and natural materials keep the heat out',[('They are very tall','Height is not the reason'),('They have no doors','Not the reason')],'Natural materials keep houses cool.'),
  F('9',2,'All houses are made of bricks.',False,'Houses can be made of mud, wood, grass and more.'),
  S('10',2,'What is a repeating design of shapes and lines called?',['pattern','a pattern','Pattern'],'A pattern repeats.'),
  M('11',3,'What did Mini use her piggy bank for?','To save money',[('To cook','A piggy bank saves money'),('To store water','A piggy bank saves money')],'A gullak is a clay piggy bank.'),
  M('12',3,'Which is a step before baking a pot?','Shaping it on the wheel',[('Selling it','Baking comes before selling'),('Using it','Baking comes before using')],'Shape first, then dry and bake.')],
 keep=['kiln','mould','pattern'])
